{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqqvw755vf0","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"AST code edges (calls/imports) persist as a SEPARATE overlay.code_edges array, never the task `edges` array, so they stay out of the DAG scheduler, dup judge, and spreading-activation traversal (mirrors how code_nodes is its own map). Edge shape: { from_file, to (code_node key code:<file>#<name>) | to_file, kind:'calls'|'imports', name?, ambiguous? }. Resolver (lib/code-extract/resolve-edges.js, pure/deterministic): call edge from=file,to=callee-name resolves to ALL repo code_nodes defining that name (ambiguous:true when >1; no local def => dropped, counted external); local import edge fans to the imported file's EXPORTED symbols, falling back to a single file-level edge (to_file) when the imported file has no exports; external imports dropped. `from` stays the FILE because the extractor attributes calls only file-granularly. Persistence: graph-store events code_edge_added/code_edge_removed keyed on a synthetic codeedge:<from_file> container node (stripped from graph.nodes on load via\n\n[Long raw evidence preserved as structured source chunks.]","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T17:06:44.601Z"}
